<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles XIII of Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1748">1748</a>–<a href="/years/1818">1818</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Charles II of Norway</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles XIII was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from 1809, after the deposition of his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-iv-adolf">Gustav IV Adolf</a>, and King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> from November 1814. Childless, he adopted the French marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xiv-john">Jean-Baptiste Bernadotte</a> as heir. During his reign Sweden briefly held Guadeloupe, granted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1813, and the union of Sweden and Norway began.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-xiii-of-sweden.jpg" alt="Charles XIII of Sweden" width="320" height="367" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Frederik von Breda · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Charles_XIII_of_Sweden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
